            <ArticleTitle>Intermittent back pain after central venous catheter placement.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>91-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of inadvertent azygos placement of a central venous catheter. The patient experienced ill-defined back pain associated with total parenteral nutrition infusion. The catheter malposition remained unrecognized and resulted in extensive diagnostic work-up. Symptoms resolved after the catheter was withdrawn.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
